# PROVENANCE

from loom 898d0432006545d176641053c4c1187033441791, library as of 2026-11-24

Every folder under `loom/` here was written by `deno task library:publish` in the loom
repository, at the commit above, on that date. It has TWO sources, and neither of them is this
repository:

    the 18 entry folders
        <- loom `library.pin.json` at the commit above, which pins https://github.com/loombot-ai/library at
           01a400cae11168aded286972110c0bdb4cad9bbb
    the 8 folders that carry a program loom RUNS
        <- `loom/library/<folder>/` at the commit above (browser-for-online-tasks, building-a-loom-app, file-viewer, mcp, task-board, web-search, writing-a-tool-module, writing-payloads-in-repl-code)

`README.md` and `LICENSE.md` at this repository's root are its own editorial files. The publish does not
write them, and it refuses to run in a checkout that has neither.

Nothing under `loom/` is edited by hand: a change made here is a change the next publish
deletes.

## How to check one file against the commit above

A folder loom runs - its bytes are that commit's `loom/library/` folder, byte for byte:

    git -C <a loom checkout> show <commit>:loom/library/<folder>/<file> \
      | diff - loom/<folder>/<file>

An entry - its authority is the pinned commit, so the check is that the pin still names it:

    git -C <a loom checkout> show <commit>:library.pin.json        # names 01a400cae11168aded286972110c0bdb4cad9bbb

and then, in that loom checkout, `deno task library:publish --dry`: it re-reads the pinned cache and
these folders, compares every file the public tree should hold, and prints `nothing to change` on a tree
that agrees with its sources. That dry run is the whole check, and it is one command.
